00:09:43,923 --> 00:09:45,530
politics.

293
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:47,129
When power is cheap,

294
00:09:47,129 --> 00:09:49,590
voters notice who gets it.

295
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:53,010
Norway moved to block new crypto mines.

296
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:55,480
Quebec decides who plugs in.

297
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:58,092
Ireland makes newcomers bring their own

298
00:09:58,092 --> 00:09:59,110
power.

299
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:01,843
Texas passed a law letting the grid

300
00:10:01,843 --> 00:10:03,878
tell giant users to cut back in

301
00:10:03,878 --> 00:10:05,750
an emergency.

302
00:10:06,090 --> 00:10:07,867
Cheap electricity,

303
00:10:07,867 --> 00:10:08,871
it turns out,

304
00:10:08,871 --> 00:10:11,163
is a resource governments guard,

305
00:10:11,163 --> 00:10:12,536
just like oil.

306
00:10:16,984 --> 00:10:19,664
Let me draw the big difference.

307
00:10:19,884 --> 00:10:22,434
Oil made one world market.

308
00:10:22,564 --> 00:10:24,905
A barrel costs roughly the same wherever

309
00:10:24,905 --> 00:10:25,735
you buy it,

310
00:10:25,735 --> 00:10:26,974
plus shipping.

311
00:10:26,984 --> 00:10:29,455
So oil money flowed to whoever owned

312
00:10:29,455 --> 00:10:30,504
the wells.

313
00:10:30,734 --> 00:10:33,553
Electricity makes lots of little local

314
00:10:33,553 --> 00:10:34,182
markets,

315
00:10:34,182 --> 00:10:36,734
each one stuck behind its own wires.

316
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:38,495
So the prize doesn't go to whoever

317
00:10:38,495 --> 00:10:40,334
has the most energy.

318
00:10:40,354 --> 00:10:43,018
It goes to whoever can deliver it

319
00:10:43,018 --> 00:10:43,524
fast,

320
00:10:43,524 --> 00:10:44,563
in huge blocks,

321
00:10:44,563 --> 00:10:46,228
and keep it on.

322
00:10:46,484 --> 00:10:46,900
So,

323
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,305
could cheap electricity become the new

324
00:10:49,305 --> 00:10:50,084
oil?

325
00:10:50,084 --> 00:10:51,166
In one way,

326
00:10:51,166 --> 00:10:51,994
yes.

327
00:10:51,994 --> 00:10:54,447
Just like oil a century ago,

328
00:10:54,447 --> 00:10:56,430
it's deciding where the next giant

329
00:10:56,430 --> 00:10:57,644
industries land,

330
00:10:57,644 --> 00:11:00,371
and countries are already competing for

331
00:11:00,371 --> 00:11:01,337
them with dams,

332
00:11:01,337 --> 00:11:03,424
solar fields and tax deals.

333
00:11:03,554 --> 00:11:04,392
But in another way,

334
00:11:04,392 --> 00:11:04,724
no.

335
00:11:04,724 --> 00:11:07,824
Oil could be shipped to anyone.

336
00:11:07,854 --> 00:11:09,822
Electricity has to be used close to

337
00:11:09,822 --> 00:11:10,794
where it's made.

338
00:11:10,794 --> 00:11:12,583
So the new oil isn't just cheap

339
00:11:12,583 --> 00:11:13,694
power.

340
00:11:13,724 --> 00:11:15,771
It's cheap power you can plug into

341
00:11:15,771 --> 00:11:16,204
now,

342
00:11:16,204 --> 00:11:18,251
and that a country is willing to

343
00:11:18,251 --> 00:11:19,078
share.

344
00:11:19,317 --> 00:11:22,397
So who's winning right now?

345
00:11:22,567 --> 00:11:24,372
The cold hydro north,

346
00:11:24,372 --> 00:11:26,807
for the giant training halls.

347
00:11:27,047 --> 00:11:27,713
Texas and the Gulf,

348
00:11:27,713 --> 00:11:28,597
for speed and scale.

349
00:11:28,597 --> 00:11:29,714
Quebec,

350
00:11:29,714 --> 00:11:33,397
if you can get its permission.

351
00:11:33,477 --> 00:11:34,068
Brazil,

352
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,699
if it can make its power bill

353
00:11:35,699 --> 00:11:36,707
lighter.

354
00:11:36,877 --> 00:11:38,337
And the losers?

355
00:11:38,347 --> 00:11:40,863
Places with cheap power and a grid

356
00:11:40,863 --> 00:11:43,140
that can't take one more plug.

357
00:11:43,384 --> 00:11:45,534
Nia files her report.

358
00:11:45,534 --> 00:11:46,507
Not one pin,

359
00:11:46,507 --> 00:11:48,094
but a pattern.

360
00:11:48,094 --> 00:11:50,620
The giant training halls go where power

361
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:53,184
is cheap and cold air is free.

362
00:11:53,214 --> 00:11:55,014
The answering machines stay near the

363
00:11:55,014 --> 00:11:55,874
cities.

364
00:11:55,874 --> 00:11:57,906
And the winners are the places that

365
00:11:57,906 --> 00:12:00,764
build wires as fast as data centers.

366
00:12:00,864 --> 00:12:03,064
Cubby finally gets its plug.

367
00:12:03,064 --> 00:12:05,754
And Nia gets her next assignment.

368
00:12:05,754 --> 00:12:08,900
Find the plug for the robot factories.

369
00:12:09,150 --> 00:12:09,809
Next time,

370
00:12:09,809 --> 00:12:12,762
we follow the money behind another hidden

371
00:12:12,762 --> 00:12:15,170
link of the world economy.

372
00:12:15,170 --> 00:12:17,541
This is The Hidden Economics.
